{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>For a generation of reversals, etc.</b> That is, because the verse said just before, ״אַסְתִּירָה פָנַי״ and so forth — and by this He would not look and see even if they repent and their voice cries out for mercy — and this is not proper to do, therefore the speaker concluded, ״כִּי דוֹר תַּהְפֻּכוֹת״ — meaning, they turn from good to evil. And His saying ״בָּנִים״ — meaning, even if they think to better themselves by coming to the fence so that they would be counted as sons — ״לֹא אֵמֻן בָּם״, for they will return to wickedness and their return is not whole, and therefore it is fitting to hide, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:27.802651346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}